# Session 4: 1807 (the scenario starts in October 1806), one player, the Allies (the shipped
# NWS.CFG), Tactical off. The scenario's start and its end (docs\won-source-study.md, section 3.2).
seed 1
pace 1

wait 4
key space
wait 4
key s
wait 2
key down down
wait 1
shot start-year
key enter
wait 3
shot objective
key space
wait 1
key u t esc
wait 1
shot main-menu

# The start: the end conditions and the force summary.
key u e
wait 1
shot end-cond
key esc
wait 1
key esc
wait 1
key i down down down enter
wait 1
shot force-summary
key space
wait 1

# The Allies only end their turns. Each turn: end it, wait for the French moves, then
# spaces to close the messages. At the main menu, and at the menus below that wait for a
# choice, a space matches no item and is dropped.
repeat 6
key e y
wait 30
shot turn-end
repeat 16
key space
wait 2
end
shot next-turn
end

# September 1807. Napoleon beats Hohenlohe at Minsk, and the player chooses where
# Hohenlohe retreats.
key e y
wait 30
shot turn-end
repeat 16
key space
wait 2
end
shot retreat
key f
wait 3
repeat 16
key space
wait 2
end
shot next-turn

# Friedland, the Allies' objective, falls, and the game offers to end. The player
# overrides, to play on to the time limit.
key e y
wait 30
shot turn-end
repeat 16
key space
wait 2
end
shot end-game
key n
wait 3
shot override

# Four more turns. In the last, July 1808, time runs out and the game offers to end
# again. France has 620 VP, a new high score; the computer's entry is named COMPUTER.
repeat 4
key e y
wait 30
shot turn-end
repeat 16
key space
wait 2
end
shot next-turn
end
key y
wait 3
shot battle-summary
key space
wait 8
# The Hall of Fame, then "Game Over" below it.
shot hall-of-fame
key space
wait 5
shot start-menu
key q
wait 3
shot dos
